[BEGIN]: The facility monitoring system handles failures through a robust, multi-layered failure management process. It continuously aggregates sensor data across thermal, acoustic, and vibration channels, correlating anomalies across domains. To mitigate transient noise, it applies threshold logic with hysteresis, ensuring only persistent deviations trigger escalation. Persistent deviations are escalated to the on-call responder for immediate action. Every decision is logged in an append-only audit trail for accountability and forensic review. Additionally, the system reconciles clock drift between distributed edge devices to maintain consistent event ordering during incident analysis. This comprehensive approach ensures reliable failure detection, timely escalation, and traceable, tamper-proof postmortem analysis.[END]
